#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""whackagent backlog provider: code on GitHub, tickets on a board.

Implements the operations in providers/CONTRACT.md on top of `gh`. Stdlib only, one file: projects
vendor it as is (`.github/board/wa-backlog`). `providers/github/wa-backlog` links here.
Settings come from repository variables (shared with the board workflow), IDs are
cached per clone in <git-common-dir>/whackagent/github-cache.json.

Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 error · 2 usage · 3 claim taken · 4 wrong state for the operation.

Shared core (same for every board): CLI, verbs, states, claim-from rules, exit codes, claims (git refs
on the GitHub repo), ticket branches and task phases, pull requests, merge, stacks, screenshots, the
contract check, `hook`, the board hooks of a board other than GitHub (GitHub events → board writes), and `migrate` (GitHub board → Plane). Everything the board tool owns sits behind `Board`, picked by `backlog.provider`
in .whackagent/config.md: `github` (a GitHub Project v2) or `plane` (a Plane Community Edition project,
experimental); anything else falls back to GitHub. The Plane API key comes from env PLANE_API_KEY only.

Board interface: one adapter class per board tool. Tickets are dicts: number (the ticket id: an issue
number, or a board key "WA-42"), title, summary, state, column, size, sprint, milestone, closed,
not_planned, ignored, assignees, reserved, claims (filled by the core), url, item_id; a card that is
not a ticket is {"draft": True, "title", "item_id"}. An operation a tool has no meaning for keeps the
base method, which exits 2 with a clear message. A ticket id of the other board's shape exits 2 too.

  Reading     check_id(number)            refuse an id of the wrong shape before any call (12 vs "WA-42")
              settings(repo, variables)   board ids resolved from the repo variables, cached with the config
              tickets()                   every card, priority order (`list`, `claims` filter it)
              get(number)                 one ticket, read fresh; a ticket missing from the board is added
              blocked_by(number)          blockers, [{number, state}]
              me()                        the account a claim assigns, `reserved` compares against
              assigned_to_me(ticket)      that account already among the ticket's assignees
  Writing     set_state(ticket, state)    move the card to a state's column
              move(number, before, after, bottom)    priority: top when all empty
              set_size(ticket, size)
              assign(number, login) / unassign(number, login)    claim reservation; assign → success
              comment(number, text)
              cancel(ticket)              closed as not planned: off the board, never claimable, not done
              create(title, body, milestone, size, sprint)    → {number, url, milestone}, card in todo
  Milestones  milestones()                release scopes, highest first, [{title, open, tickets, done}]
              close_milestone(title) / set_milestone(number, title)
  Sprints     split(ticket, name)         ticket becomes the root of sprint <name>, off the board
              set_sprint(number, sprint)  sprint membership, "" detaches
  Other       depend(number, blockers)    → (added, already there)
              link_pr(number, pr)         the pull request linked on the ticket (GitHub: closing link, Plane: card link)
              provision(args, repo)       create or adopt the board, write the repo variables → report
              check_integration(args, repo)    the tool's own GitHub sync off? (single writer) → report
              templates(owner)            board templates provision can copy
              ticket_url(number)
"""

